NASA/JPL DE440 and PLU060 ephemeris data

The Moon and Pluto coefficient arrays in Sources/CLibAstronomy/EphemerisData
were derived by Heirloom Logic from NASA/JPL planetary and satellite
ephemerides obtained from the official NAIF distribution. The Swift table
Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Moon/Generated/MoonDE440Coefficients.swift is
generated from moon_data.inc and holds the same Moon coefficients, and the
Swift tables PlutoBarycenterCoefficients.swift, PlutoSunCoefficients.swift
and PlutoCenterCoefficients.swift in Sources/AstronomyKit/Engine/Gravity/Generated
are generated from the three pluto_*.inc files and hold the same Pluto
coefficients:

  de440s.bsp, JPL planetary and lunar ephemeris DE440, integrated 25 June 2020
  https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/planets/de440s.bsp
  SHA-256 c1c7feeab882263fc493a9d5a5b2ddd71b54826cdf65d8d17a76126b260a49f2

  plu060.bsp, PLU060 satellite ephemeris with Pluto barycenter, Sun,
  Earth-Moon barycenter and Earth from DE440 (BVS/NAIF, 3 April 2024)
  https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/spk/satellites/plu060.bsp
  SHA-256 dfbb102491a26ed41ae08ca3f8963f22f0219df1d8f265ab87b9ad825a826fc6

Heirloom Logic is responsible for the subtraction, unit conversion,
coefficient selection, serialization and integration in AstronomyKit. The
derived arrays are not official JPL SPK kernels. This package ships derived
numeric coefficients and its own evaluator; it does not ship the CSPICE
toolkit.

Reference: R.S. Park, W.M. Folkner, J.G. Williams, and D.H. Boggs, The JPL
Planetary and Lunar Ephemerides DE440 and DE441, Astronomical Journal 161, 105
(2021), DOI 10.3847/1538-3881/abd414.

